title: gamescript
---
<<declare $YarnTalkedElder = false>>
	Josh: There's more mist than usual...
===

title: square_initial
---
	Josh: What's up Elder Amos?
	Elder Amos: Hmm, fine, fine indeed. I'm fine, yes. How about you, young one?
	Josh: I'm good. Kind of a misty day, don't you think?
	Elder Amos: Yes, the mist. The mist is strong. I- very good. 
	-> Uh... what's very good?
		Josh: Uh... what's very good?
		Elder Amos: Yes, indeed. Very good.
	-> Yup. Very good...?
		Josh: Yup. Very good...?
		Elder Amos: The mist. Very good. It's strong. Very good.
	Josh: Ok... good talk, I guess.
	Josh: ... I swear this geezer wasn't as weird a few days ago.
	<<set $YarnTalkedElder = true>>
===
title: square_marcus_erika
---
	Marcus: What's up Joshy?
	Josh: 'Sup.
	Erika: Wow, look who's in a good mood today.
	Josh: Yup, brimmin' with joy.
	Marcus: Ah, come on Joshy it's a beautiful day! Everyone's having fun, doing their things... a little misty, but beautiful anyway.
	Josh: You have a weird concept of beauty.
	<<if $YarnTalkedElder is true>>
		Josh: Anyway... have you talked to Elder Amos? He seems to be out of it.
		Marcus: Ah, old man's always been like this, nothing new.
		Josh: I don't know man, he seems worse.
		Erika: Screw that fossil, what are we doing today?
	<<else>>
		Erika: So, what are we doing today?
	<<endif>>
	Josh: I'm heading home I guess.
	Marcus: Come on Joshy, you know I don't have much time...
	Josh: He's really leaving, then.
	Erika: Don't be a shut in for once, Josh.
	Josh: Ok ok. I'll just relax for a bit, and I'll meet you.
	Marcus: Nice, okay.
	Erika: We meet here in an hour-ish.
	Josh: 'Kay.
	<<progress TalkedFriends>>
===
title: not_talked_friends
---
Josh: Hmm... Maybe I should go see my friends before heading home. We haven't talked in a bit.
<<progress NotTalkedFriendsYet>>
===
title: home_outside_first
---
<<movement JoshApproach>>
Josh: What's this?! 
<<face Josh left>>
<<enable HazeOne>>
<<movement HazeFloatDown flip freeze>>
...
<<movement HazeEnter flip freeze>>
Haze: Hm... Hello sir.
Josh: Wha—who... what are you?!
Haze: Hmm... I'm me I guess, I don't know.
Josh: Okay..? And what are you doing here?
Haze: Nothing in particular.
Josh: Okay just— come inside or else you'll freak people out.
Haze: Why would I freak them out?
Josh: Have you looked at yourself in the mirror?
<<movement HazeApproach freeze>>
Haze: I... haven't.
Josh: Yeah, figures.
Haze: But you're not freaked out?
Josh: You don't seem hostile.
Haze: I don't feel hostile.
Josh: Just come on in man.
<<movement HazeRun flip freeze>>
<<movement HazeLeave flip freeze>>
<<disable HazeOne>>
Josh: (This is gonna be a long day...)
<<progress MetHaze>>
===

title: home_inside_first
---
<<enable HazeTwo>>
<<movement JoshHouse freeze>>
<<movement HazeHouse freeze>>
Haze: Wow your home is so pretty!
Josh: It really isn't.
<<movement HazeWander1>>
Haze: Then why are you here?
Josh: Nowhere to go, I guess.
<<movement HazeWander2 flip>>
Haze: That's sad.
<<movement HazeWander3 flip>>
Haze: What's this?
Josh: That's a TV.
<<movement HazeTV flip>>
Haze: What does it do?
Josh: Shows moving images.
Haze: Isn't that basically everything already?
Josh: "Everything" is not engaging enough, I guess.
<<movement HazeWander1>>
Haze: You're weird.
Josh: I'm weird? Says the orange floating thing that appeared out of nowhere. Look— who are you anyway, man? Why are you even here?
Haze: As I said, I don't know!
Josh: I'm guessing you don't have a name, also.
<<movement HazeWander2 flip>>
Haze: Not that I can remember, no.
Josh: Okay then. I'll call you Haze for now. Call me Josh.
<<movement HazeWander1 flip>>
Haze: ...ok.
Josh: So, you really have no idea how you wound up here?
Haze: Nuh uh. I feel like I just woke up from a really long nap. Like, reeeeally long.
Josh: Like, how long?
Haze: Feels like it's been forever since I fell asleep, honestly.
Josh: And you just suddenly fell asleep like that? For like, what, ages?
<<movement HazeTV>>
Haze: I'm trying to remember, but it's all too messy in my hea—
<<movement HazeWander2 freeze>>
Josh: Now what?
Haze: Ugh!
Josh: What?
<<movement HazeWander1 flip>>
Haze: Felt... something.
Josh: What?
Haze: Pain. But it's gone now.
Josh: ...Ok, good. I'm gonna watch some TV then.
Haze: I'm gonna go for a walk!
<<movement HazeExit freeze>>
<<disable HazeTwo>>
Josh: No you're not, you'll stand out and freak out every—hey, WAIT!
<<progress HazeRanOff>>
<<enable HazeThree>>
===

title: square_haze
---
Josh: HEY, wa— huff... huff... wait. Are you insane? Do I have to remind you you're not human?
Haze: Relax my friend, I found something out! Look.
<<movement HazeStand flip freeze>>
Haze: Ta-dah!
Josh: ...
Haze: ...
Josh: You know nothing happened right.
Haze: Well, for you it didn't, but that's because you're the only one who can see me right now!
Josh: What? Stop this nonsense dude. Come back to my house and stay there.
<<movement JoshWalk freeze>>
<<face JoshTwo right>>
Haze: ...
Josh: ...
<<enable Villager>>
<<movement VillagerEnter freeze>>
Villager: Josh! What are you doing just standing here?
Josh: Uhm... nothing really, I was just... taking a walk. Yes, a walk.
Villager: Taking a walk? Are you insane? Can't you hear the noise coming from elder Amos' house?
Josh: Oh, yeah. So that's where all the ruckus' coming from.
Villager: Yeah. Anyway, meet everyone there then, after you finish your... walk or whatever. Hurry.
<<movement VillagerExit>>
Haze: Turns out you're the insane one.
Josh: Shut up.
Haze: Trust me now?
Josh: For this very specific topic, yes.
Haze: Can I go, then?
<<disable Villager>>
<<disable HazeThree>>
<<enable TrueHaze>>
Josh: ...okay.
===

title: elders_house_outside
---
Erika: Hey slowpoke.
Marcus: Joshy!
Josh: Hey guys, what happened?
Erika: Basically, elder Amos disappeared. People are saying they saw him go into the forest, speaking nonsense.
Josh: Into the forest where, exactly?
Marcus: No one saw exactly, spot was too misty, apparently.
Haze: ...
Marcus: They are scared, afraid to enter his house. Some saying it's cursed.
Josh: What? No one went looking for him?
Erika: They did, but didn't go very far.
Haze: Josh, I feel like we should go in.
Josh: Are you really inside my mind, man?
Haze: Don't ask me how. Let's go in.
Josh: Ok, why?
Haze: Just trust me on this one, I feel like there's something there worth finding.
Josh: ...ok.
Josh: Ok, I guess I'm going to check his place, then.
Erika: What, why?
Marcus: What could be inside?
Josh: I don't know, man. You two have a better idea?
Erika: Why are you so proactive out of nowhere?
Marcus: Who are you and where is our friend Josh?
Haze: Haha!
Josh: Funny. Kay, I'm going in.
Erika: I'm going in then, also.
Marcus: Yeah, me too.
Haze: Would be better if we went by ourselves.
Josh: Why? It doesn't matter anyway. I won't stop my friends.
Haze: ..ok.
Josh: Let's go, then.
===

title: elders_house_inside_explore
---
Josh: What are we looking for, exactly?
Haze: No idea.
Josh: Great.
Marcus: Hmm, food's still good, yeah.
Erika: A Bible... I am out of rolling paper.
===

title: elders_house_bookshelf
---
Haze: Books! Let's see here... "Suddenly, he sits up and tugs my panties off and throws them on the floor. Pulling off his boxer briefs, his erecti—"
Josh: Ok, ok, that's enough.
===

title: elders_house_wardrobe
---
Haze: Anything there?
Josh: Nope, it's a mess, I couldn't find anything useful if I really wanted to.
===

title: elders_house_writing_table
---
Haze: What are these? Notes?
Josh: Let's see...
Josh: It's been calling to me, calling to me sometime now, calling to me... WHAT SHOULD I DO WHAT SHOULD I DO HELP HELP HELP I NEED TO GO THERE, I NEED TO FIND IT, I NEED TO GET IT IT'S THE ONLY WAY ONLY I CAN DO IT... only I know about it.
Josh: Holy fuck, he was really losing it. What is he talking about?
Haze: There's more down there.
Josh: It's a poem... I can barely read it, must be ages-old.
Josh: North you must go
To get what you need
Through the dark forest path
A new site you shall see
Solve the riddles therein
Before time runs out
Or else for the land
Ruin will befall
Josh: Huh... Riddles? What is this, a game? Why was this geezer fooling around with this?
Haze: I guess we need to go North and find out, no?
Josh: I don't know. Do I need to find anything out? As far as I know a senile old man got lost in the forest. The only really weird thing here is still you.
Josh: Which leads me to think... do you have anything to do with all this?
Haze: ...I might, but I'm not sure. I really feel like we need to follow this trail.
Josh: Ok, then, let's check it out. I'll talk to Erika and Mark.
Haze: Is it wise to tell them? It might blow my cover.
Josh: Well, they are my best—actually, only, friends. I'd rather be close to them if anything's happening around here. Besides, they would like you, I think.
Haze: Would they?! Ok then, let's go!
Josh: Don't get too excited, an old man just disappeared.
Haze: Oh, yes, of course. That's so sad, I'm sorry.
Josh: Nahh I'm just messing with you man.
Haze: ...
===

title: elders_house_first_floor
---
Josh: Kay guys, I found something, look.
Marcus: Damn, seems like he was really losing it.
Erika: Holy...
Erika: Ok, so what, we should head North... isn't that the forest path right behind this house?
Josh: Yup.
Marcus: I didn't think there was a path there.
Josh: Let's see, maybe we find one.
Marcus: At least it's something to do!
Erika: Yeah, if it kills our boredom...
Josh: ...
===

title: forest_path
---
Marcus: Huh, what do you know? There was really a path!
Erika: Can this even be called a path?
===

title: graveyard
---
Erika: Holy...
Marcus: How was this hidden here all along?
Haze: Did you know about this place, Josh?
Josh: Nope. I know as much as them.
===

title: puzzle_entrance
---
Erika: What the hell is this?
Josh: Probably one of the riddles the poem mentioned.
Marcus: Meh, I suck at puzzles.
Erika: Same. This one's on you, Josh.
Josh: Huh, it's that same statue from Elder's.
Haze: I feel it calling to me.
Erika: What? How did you do that?
Marcus: Way to go Joshy!
Haze: Seems they didn't notice me...
===

